(>> 2.1 The Empathize Phase: Moving Beyond Sympathy) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Empathy is the deliberate, non-judgmental immersion into the lived experiences,) Tj
T*
(emotional states, physical contexts, and underlying values of users.) Tj
T*
(* Sympathy vs Empathy: Sympathy expresses passive pity from an external distance \('I) Tj
T*
(feel sorry for your hardship'\). Empathy actively shares and internalizes the user's) Tj
T*
(worldview and emotional reality \('I feel and experience what you feel'\).) Tj
T*
(* Computational Empathy in Software Engineering: Designing intuitive user) Tj
T*
(experiences, accessibility features for individuals with sensory/motor impairments,) Tj
T*
(and error tolerance that anticipates human cognitive limits rather than blaming user) Tj
T*
(error.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 2.2 Qualitative and Quantitative User Research Methodologies) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Quantitative Research: Answers 'What?', 'How much?', and 'How often?' through) Tj
T*
(analytics dashboards, telemetry logs, A/B test data, and structured surveys. Provides) Tj
T*
(statistical validation over large sample cohorts.) Tj
T*
(* Qualitative Research: Answers 'Why?' and 'How do users feel?' through open-ended) Tj
T*
(semi-structured interviews, direct ethnographic observation, and context mapping.) Tj
T*
(Reveals deep emotional drivers, hidden workarounds, and implicit needs.) Tj
T*
(* The 5 Whys Root-Cause Protocol: Developed by Sakichi Toyoda for the Toyota) Tj
T*
(Production System; repeatedly interrogates causal chains by asking 'Why?' five times) Tj
T*
(to peel away superficial symptoms and expose the foundational root failure.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 2.3 The AEIOU Observational Framework) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(The AEIOU framework structures field ethnographic observations into five distinct) Tj
T*
(analytical categories:) Tj
T*
(* Activities: Specific actions and goal-directed workflows users perform \(e.g.) Tj
T*
(searching for a course, entering passwords\).) Tj
T*
(* Environments: The physical and digital contexts where activities occur \(e.g. noisy) Tj
T*
(outdoor subway, dim hospital ward, mobile network dead-zone\).) Tj
T*
(* Interactions: Direct touchpoints between people, people and machines, or machines) Tj
T*
(and physical spaces.) Tj
T*
(* Objects: Physical and digital tools, devices, documents, and makeshift workarounds) Tj
T*
(users engage with.) Tj
T*
