([CASE STUDY 4: Reframing 'How Might We' for Public Bus Transit App]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: Commuters in a metropolitan city complained that public buses were) Tj
T*
(always late, causing crowded platforms and passenger anger.) Tj
T*
(Generating and Tuning HMW Questions:) Tj
T*
(Initial Poor HMW \(Too Narrow\): How might we make all city buses run on time?) Tj
T*
(\(Engineering team cannot alter city traffic congestion\).) Tj
T*
(Initial Poor HMW \(Too Broad\): How might we solve city urban transportation? \(Too) Tj
T*
(massive; un-actionable\).) Tj
T*
(Balanced Actionable HMWs:) Tj
T*
(- HMW 1: How might we provide commuters with real-time GPS bus location tracking so) Tj
T*
(waiting feels predictable and manageable?) Tj
T*
(- HMW 2: How might we transform waiting time at bus stops into a productive or enjoyable) Tj
T*
(social experience?) Tj
T*
(- HMW 3: How might we incentivize commuters to shift their travel by 20 minutes to) Tj
T*
(equalize passenger loading across buses?) Tj
T*
(Winning Product Feature: Real-time crowdsourced GPS arrival countdowns displayed on bus) Tj
T*
(stop e-ink screens and mobile apps, reducing perceived waiting frustration by 65%.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 2.6 University Review & Examination Questions) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Q1: Explain the structure and utility of the AEIOU observational framework in) Tj
T*
(ethnographic user research.) Tj
T*
(Answer: The AEIOU framework is an ethnographic research protocol that structures) Tj
T*
(observational data into five interrelated dimensions: \(1\) Activities: Goal-oriented) Tj
T*
(workflows, sequential tasks, and actions users undertake. \(2\) Environments: Physical and) Tj
T*
(digital spaces, layout, acoustics, and environmental constraints. \(3\) Interactions:) Tj
T*
(Person-to-person or person-to-artifact relationships and touchpoints. \(4\) Objects:) Tj
T*
(Physical devices, software tools, forms, and improvised workarounds. \(5\) Users:) Tj
T*
(Demographic traits, roles, and behavioral habits. By categorizing field notes into) Tj
T*
(AEIOU, designers prevent cognitive bias, spot unarticulated user frustrations, and) Tj
T*
